WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:04.600
The world is charged with the grandeur of
God.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.300
It will flame out, like shining from shook
foil;

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.100
It gathers to a greatness, like the ooze of
oil

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.950
Crushed. Why do men then now not reck his
rod?

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:22.950
Generations have trod, have trod, have trod;
And all is seared with trade; bleared, smeared

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.900
with toil;
And bears man’s smudge and shares man’s

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:33.910
smell: the soil
Is bare now, nor can foot feel, being shod.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:40.320
And yet for all this, nature is never spent;
There lives the dearest freshness deep down

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.149
things;
And though the last lights off the black West

00:00:44.149 --> 00:00:49.469
went
Ah, morning, at the brown brink eastward,

00:00:49.469 --> 00:00:53.129
springs—
Because the Holy Ghost over the bent

00:00:53.129 --> 00:00:59.189
World broods with warm breast and with ah!
bright wings.

